               1                     !> \defgroup SAMF_shal Scale-Aware Mass-Flux Shallow Convection
               2                     !! @{
               3                     !!  \brief The scale-aware mass-flux shallow (SAMF_shal) convection scheme is an updated version of the previous mass-flux shallow convection scheme with scale and aerosol awareness and parameterizes the effect of shallow convection on the environment.  T
               4                     !!
               5                     !!  The previous version of the shallow convection scheme (shalcnv.f) is described in Han and Pan (2011) \cite han_and_pan_2011 and differences between the shallow and deep convection schemes are presented in Han and Pan (2011) \cite han_and_pan_2011 and
               6                     !!
               7                     !!  \section diagram Calling Hierarchy Diagram
               8                     !!  \image html SAMF_shal_Flowchart.png "Diagram depicting how the SAMF shallow convection scheme is called from the FV3GFS physics time loop" height=2cm
               9                     !!  \section intraphysics Intraphysics Communication
              10                     !!  This space is reserved for a description of how this scheme uses information from other scheme types and/or how information calculated in this scheme is used in other scheme types.
              11                     
              12                     !> \file samfshalcnv.f
              13                     !!  Contains the entire SAMF shallow convection scheme.
              14                     
              15                     !>  \brief This subroutine contains the entirety of the SAMF shallow convection scheme.
              16                     !!
              17                     !!  This routine follows the \ref SAMF deep scheme quite closely, although it can be interpreted as only having the "static" and "feedback" control portions, since the "dynamic" control is not necessary to find the cloud base mass flux. The algorithm is s
              18                     !!
              19                     !!  \param[in] im number of used points
              20                     !!  \param[in] ix horizontal dimension
              21                     !!  \param[in] km vertical layer dimension
              22                     !!  \param[in] jcap number of spectral wave trancation
              23                     !!  \param[in] delt physics time step in seconds
              24                     !!  \param[in] delp pressure difference between level k and k+1 (Pa)
              25                     !!  \param[in] prslp mean layer presure (Pa)
              26                     !!  \param[in] psp surface pressure (Pa)
              27                     !!  \param[in] phil layer geopotential (\f$m^s/s^2\f$)
              28                     !!  \param[inout] ql cloud water (kg/kg)
              29                     !!  \param[inout] qi cloud ice (kg/kg)
              30                     !!  \param[inout] q1 updated tracers (kg/kg)
              31                     !!  \param[inout] t1 updated temperature (K)
              32                     !!  \param[inout] u1 updated zonal wind (\f$m s^{-1}\f$)
              33                     !!  \param[inout] v1 updated meridional wind (\f$m s^{-1}\f$)
              34                     !!  \param[out] rn convective rain (m)
              35                     !!  \param[out] kbot index for cloud base
              36                     !!  \param[out] ktop index for cloud top
              37                     !!  \param[out] kcnv flag to denote deep convection (0=no, 1=yes)
              38                     !!  \param[in] islimsk sea/land/ice mask (=0/1/2)
              39                     !!  \param[in] dot layer mean vertical velocity (Pa/s)
              40                     !!  \param[in] ncloud number of cloud species
              41                     !!  \param[in] hpbl PBL height (m)
              42                     !!  \param[in] heat surface sensible heat flux (K m/s)
              43                     !!  \param[in] evap surface latent heat flux (kg/kg m/s)
              44                     !!  \param[out] ud_mf updraft mass flux multiplied by time step (\f$kg/m^2\f$)
              45                     !!  \param[out] dt_mf ud_mf at cloud top (\f$kg/m^2\f$)
              46                     !!  \param[out] cnvw convective cloud water (kg/kg)
              47                     !!  \param[out] cnvc convective cloud cover (unitless)
              48                     !!  \param[in] clam coefficient for entrainment rate
              49                     !!  \param[in] c0s convective rain conversion parameter (1/m)
              50                     !!  \param[in] c1 conversion parameter of detrainment from liquid water into grid-scale cloud water (1/m)
              51                     !!  \param[in] pgcon reduction factor in momentum transport due to convection induced pressure gradient force
              52                     !!  \param[in] asolfac aerosol-aware parameter inversely proportional to CCN number concentraion
              53                     !!
              54                     !!  \section general General Algorithm
              55                     !!  -# Compute preliminary quantities needed for the static and feedback control portions of the algorithm.
              56                     !!  -# Perform calculations related to the updraft of the entraining/detraining cloud model ("static control").
              57                     !!  -# The cloud base mass flux is obtained using the cumulus updraft velocity averaged ove the whole cloud depth.
              58                     !!  -# Calculate the tendencies of the state variables (per unit cloud base mass flux) and the cloud base mass flux.
              59                     !!  -# For the "feedback control", calculate updated values of the state variables by multiplying the cloud base mass flux and the tendencies calculated per unit cloud base mass flux from the static control.
              60                     !!  \section detailed Detailed Algorithm
              61                     !!  @{
